  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the probabilities of the minimum outcomes of each lottery and prefers the one with the lower probability of its minimum outcome. In this case, the reason would favor Lottery B (50% chance of -3000) over Lottery A (100% chance of +1000), because 50% < 100% — even though the minimum outcome of B is worse, the reason only cares about the likelihood of the minimum. However, the individual chose Lottery A based on its certainty and guaranteed gain. The individual did not consider the 'probability of the minimum outcome' as a decision variable, nor did they compare how likely the worst outcome is in each lottery. Instead, they emphasized the single, positive outcome of A. There is no indication that the individual assessed what the minimum outcome of each lottery was, nor its probability, in a comparative way. Therefore, the reasoning process described does not align with the decision reason. The individual’s focus is on certainty and positive payoff, not on minimizing the chance of experiencing the worst possible outcome in each lottery.",
